<title>USA: EMERGENCY WEATHER CONDITIONS -  WSC - 06-FEB.</title>
<headline>EMERGENCY WEATHER CONDITIONS -  WSC - 06-FEB.</headline>
<text>
<p>Tropical Cyclone Pancho-Helinda has dissipated near 21s/81e in the Indian Ocean. This system is no longer a risk to shipping.  </p>
<p>Strong winds cover much of the northeast Atlantic and the northern North Sea at this time. Shipping in this area is at risk due to high winds and very rough seas.  </p>
<p>There are no further statements at this time.</p>
</text>
